From 15d9fbeeac4e1a0b0fe2ea6a81eb66fd80afb200 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <76759272+Cris7015@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 13:42:29 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: en751221: add TP-Link Archer XR500v v1

EN7526G package of the EN751221 family: 256 MiB DDR, 128 MiB SPI-NAND
(ESMT F50L1G41A), UART at 0x1fbf0000, the LEDs (power 6, xPON 2, WPS 7,
USB 11, LOS 24, phone 25/26, internet 28) and keys (reset 0, wifi 4,
wps 9) of the board. Same flash layout and environment as the Nokia
G-240G-E: tcboot.bin in the first MiB, UBI after it with the
environment in ubootenv/ubootenv2.

The power LED is not wired to the supply: it is GPIO 6, active low
(entry 77 of the OEM led.conf), and the OEM bootloader turns it on.
After BootROM recovery nothing does, so the board would sit with only
the Ethernet link LEDs lit. It is described with default-state = "on"
so the LED uclass lights it while probing, and bootled points at it
instead of the Internet LED. Checked on the board: with GPIO 6 put back
to input first, U-Boot drives it as an output low and "led list" shows
"green:power on".

The format_ubi_part menu entry keeps the OEM misc partition (MACs at
+0xf100, EN7570 laser calibration at +0x20000, MT7662 EEPROM at
+0xe0000) and the OEM tcboot as static volumes, so the factory data and
the way back to the stock bootloader survive the migration; the
environment derives ethaddr from the misc volume before booting. Both
are taken from dumps made under the OEM-aware Linux driver and served
over TFTP (${miscfile}, ${oembootfile}), not read with "mtd read": the
OEM kernel reaches its partitions through its own BMT, which U-Boot
does not implement, so on this board mtd read returns 0xff or garbage
and the migration would have stored that and then erased the only copy
of the factory data. Nothing is erased unless the sizes match and the
contents check out: a programmed MAC at 0xf100, the EN7570 calibration
magic 0x07050700 at 0x20094, the MT7662 EEPROM id at 0xe0000 and the
"6578" TCBoot magic at 0xc; upgrade_uboot also refuses an image without
that magic. With the one-byte bad-block marker of the F50L1G41A a plain
"mtd erase" skips only the chip's real bad blocks, so no .dontskipbad
or re-marking is needed. Tested at the prompt: load_oem_backups accepts
the real dumps and rejects a wrong file.

The old hush parser has no "( ... )" grouping ("Unknown command '('")
and bin2mac needs its size argument, so boot_openwrt and set_ethaddr
use if/then/else and pass the size; without that, booting from flash
never reached the "fit" volume and fell through to TFTP. bootfile
follows the name of the OpenWrt profile for this layout
(openwrt-airoha-en751221-tplink_archer-xr500v-v1-initramfs-kernel.bin,
airoha/openwrt#67).

CONFIG_SYS_BOOTM_LEN is 32 MiB: the OpenWrt initramfs kernels are
uncompressed legacy uImages of about 9.3 MiB, above the 8 MiB default,
and bootm fails with "Image too large: increase CONFIG_SYS_BOOTM_LEN"
and resets. The kernel loads at 0x80020000 while images are staged at
the default 0x82000000, so an image larger than ~31.9 MiB would still
have to be staged higher.

Tested on the board: migrated to this layout, U-Boot boots OpenWrt from
NAND through "ubi read fit" and bootm, and a 9705156-byte initramfs
fetched by TFTP boots through bootm as well.

